@startuml module-acceptance
!include theme.iuml
title Acceptance of a named module snapshot
start
:Record training + deployment source,\nimages, target cluster and dataset;
:Verify configuration, source availability\nand module-specific quality gates;
:Deploy and check initialization;
:Run editor HTTP and S3 smoke checks;
:Validate distributed typed CWL\nand generated documentation;
:Execute the complete learning sequence\nplus specialized runtime checks;
if (Required checks pass?) then (yes)
  :Inspect output semantics,\nreadability and scientific assertions;
else (no)
  if (Fixable module defect?) then (yes)
    :Fix on a feature branch;\nsynchronize the deployed snapshot;
    :Rerun affected gates;\nrecord only their actual results;
  else (external blocker)
    :Record blocked / skipped checks\nand preserve failure evidence;
    stop
  endif
  :Resume acceptance only after\nrequired gates and output checks pass;
endif
:Finish workloads and export\nwanted S3 artifacts;
:Run lifecycle acceptance;\nverify retained files + fresh environment;
:Verify fresh reproduction\nwhen setup or distribution changed;
:Record evidence and limitations;\ncommit reviewed changes;
:Publish source / images separately\nwhen release is authorized;
stop
@enduml
